# CHAPTER 8: WORKING PRINCIPLE

NEER operates through a sequence of power activation, wireless communication, navigation and mechanical waste collection.

Initially, the battery supplies power to the system.

The ESP32 starts and establishes the Wi-Fi control interface.

The operator connects to the control network and sends movement commands.

The ESP32 receives these commands and changes the motor control outputs.

The propulsion motors move the robot across the water surface.

When the robot reaches an area containing floating debris, the collection mechanism can be activated.

The rotating mesh assembly interacts with the floating waste and transfers the retrieved material towards the collection tray.

The waste remains in the tray until it is manually removed.

The operator can stop the robot through the control interface.

