# CHAPTER 16: CONCLUSION

NEER presents the design and development of a floating water waste collection robot integrating embedded electronics, wireless communication and mechanical engineering.

The system uses an ESP32 microcontroller for remote control, geared DC motors for propulsion and a motor-driven mesh-based assembly for floating waste collection.

The floating platform provides structural support for the electronics and mechanical components, while a dedicated tray provides temporary storage for retrieved waste.

The project demonstrates the potential of integrating accessible robotic technologies to explore practical solutions for environmental challenges.

Further development can improve the system through autonomous navigation, obstacle detection, enhanced collection mechanisms and environmental monitoring.

The prototype provides a foundation for continued experimentation and the development of more advanced floating waste collection systems.

